        "original_id": "c95797d8-0494-594f-8f25-6ee3d91820bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lancaster, Lancashire, England, Peel, Isle of Man, St Peter's Road\n- Organizations: Lancaster Cathedral, Cathedral Church of St Peter, Saint Peter's Cathedral, Peel Cathedral, Cathedral Church of Saint German, Cathedral Isle of Man\n- Concepts: Roman Catholic parish church, cathedral, parish churches, parish of the West Coast\n\nFacts:\n- Peel Cathedral, also called the Cathedral Church of Saint German and rebranded as Cathedral Isle of Man, was built in 1879–84.\n- Lancaster Cathedral was a Roman Catholic parish church until 1924, when it was elevated to cathedral status.\n- Lancaster Cathedral, also known as The Cathedral Church of St Peter and Saint Peter's Cathedral, is on St Peter's Road in Lancaster, Lancashire, England.\n- Peel Cathedral, also called the Cathedral Church of Saint German and Cathedral Isle of Man, is in Peel on the Isle of Man.\n- Peel Cathedral is also one of the parish churches in the parish of the West Coast, which includes the town of Peel.",
